    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7903a323_5b465264",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_retimer_fw_update.c",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 96,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-04T01:10:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is the deferred call needed?  pd_set_suspend() checks if the caller is running in the PD_TASK already.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 96,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 96,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "4492ffd524720f7edcbfe484b383f6688596bca7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "016598ea_d90103f6",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_retimer_fw_update.c",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 96,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-04T02:07:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "usb_retimer_fw_update_process_op_cb() is called by PD task.\npd_set_suspend() check if current task is PD task, so calling pd_set_suspend() directly from usb_retimer_fw_update_process_op_cb() causes exit early from here. So I added hook deferred call which is in different task and pd_set_suspend can run to end.\n\n/*\n\t\t * Avoid deadlock when running from task\n\t\t * which we are going to suspend\n\t\t */\n\t\tif (PD_PORT_TO_TASK_ID(port) \u003d\u003d task_get_current())\n\t\t\treturn;",
      "parentUuid": "7903a323_5b465264",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 96,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 96,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "4492ffd524720f7edcbfe484b383f6688596bca7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9d2181fc_5a1361d7",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_retimer_fw_update.c",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 96,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-04T21:19:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even with the early return, the PD task should automatically wake up after 5ms and then finish processing TC_FLAGS_REQUEST_SUSPEND. (see https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/9b2452ea/common/usbc/usbc_task.c#94)\n\nThe AP is already polling the actual suspend state using usb_retimer_fw_update_get_result()-\u003epd_is_port_enabled(), so I don\u0027t think the deferred call is needed.  I think the only result of the defer call is the PD task is woken up after 1 ms to process TC_FLAGS_REQUEST_SUSPEND instead of waiting 5 ms.  Is the AP timeout shorter than 5 ms?",
      "parentUuid": "016598ea_d90103f6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 96,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 96,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "4492ffd524720f7edcbfe484b383f6688596bca7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90058cd8_fa5c2bb4",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_retimer_fw_update.c",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 96,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-04T23:08:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right. PD task just wakes up a few ms later. AP polls result every 25ms, no side effect from early return. Functionality is the same. Just in normal exit flow, by time pd_set_suspend() returns, the caller know port is in TC_FLAGS_SUSPENDED. I felt odd when I saw early return, so I changed to hook call.\nI have changed back to call pd_set_suspend() directly.",
      "parentUuid": "9d2181fc_5a1361d7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 96,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 96,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "4492ffd524720f7edcbfe484b383f6688596bca7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
